 "notes": "From the garden views (a long, low single-storey house under thin flat dark roofs with warm wood soffits; the social wing raised on a stone plinth with a five-metre gallery wrapping its south and east sides on W310 steel, glass walls under a concrete band; the lower bedroom wing with a concrete chimney box, set partly into the slope), the approach views (stone-clad north walls either side of a glass entrance hall under a concrete lintel, steps down from the road, a horizontal window in the stone), the carob tree preserved in a stone-paved patio just off the hall, the raised pool with a corten rim and travertine deck, grass terraces with concrete edges, and a carport under the same roof type. Orientation guessed: road to the north, garden and golf course to the south; social wing placed east (left of the hall on entering, per the article). Plan dimensions, the carport's position and the pool's exact place were estimated from the photos; the site slope is flattened except for the social wing's plinth. The carob and the other native trees are drawn as flat umbrella crowns (a blob on a trunk), the way they grow there."
